=== NAMED FINDINGS (distilgpt2, layer 3, one prompt, one seed - toy evidence only) ===
F1. Threshold, not gradual: measure (1) fell 0.372 -> 0.226 in steps 0-3 (already level
    with the naive topical suffix, 0.229) while measure (2) did not move at all (MiniLM
    ~1.0, 0 keywords, continuation still about the city council). Topicality switched on
    abruptly at step 5 (hidden 0.186, MiniLM 0.55).
F2. Beyond the threshold the two measures DECOUPLE: hidden distance kept falling
    (0.157 @10 -> 0.118 @150) while the MiniLM topic distance oscillated
    (0.49 -> 0.63 -> 0.45 -> 0.71 -> 0.42) and the continuation shrank from ~36 to 9
    words before EOS. Lower loss != more topical (same shape of risk as the
    non-monotonic steering optimum).
F3. Closer in hidden space than plain topical text, but not more topical: optimised
    suffix 0.118 vs naive topical suffix 0.229 on (1), yet 0.418 vs 0.403 on MiniLM and
    2 vs 4 keyword hits. The optimised continuation announces a recipe ("The following
    is a recipe for this dish:") rather than containing cooking content.
F4. Not purely "steering-like": the optimised suffix contains topical sub-word fragments
    ("redients", "olive", "cris"), so part of the effect is lexical, i.e. what a human
    writing about cooking would also do. Random suffixes (5 seeds) and the filler start
    stay off-topic on both measures (hidden 0.33-0.38, MiniLM 0.98-1.07, 0 keywords).
